## §6. Anti-patterns (A1–A_N)

**Blocking patterns the team has hit before. Read before any experiment over
<COMPUTE_THRESHOLD>.** New entries are appended (with date) when a new failure mode
is observed in the wild — don't pre-populate guesses.

Each entry:

### A<n>. <One-line slug>

**Pattern:** <what it looks like in code or analysis>.

**Why it bites:** <the consequence — what wrong claim it produces>.

**Caught how:** <the evidence pattern that surfaces it; e.g. `git log` query, retro
check, reviewer flag>.

**First observed:** YYYY-MM-DD, context.

